{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And all the congregation murmured, saying: You, etc.</b> One needs to understand the verse's saying <b>saying</b> — since the complaint is against Moses and against Aaron, what place is there to say <b>saying</b>? Perhaps it is because the people did not say the words as written, ״אַתֶּם הֲמִתֶּם אֶת עַם ד׳״, but rather they spoke words of complaint whose overall intent was ״אַתֶּם הֲמִתֶּם״ etc.; therefore it says <b>and they murmured</b> etc., and the intent of their complaint was <b>saying</b> to them ״אַתֶּם הֲמִתֶּם״ etc." "<b>Further</b>, it may intend to raise another point — how plastered over were their eyes from seeing, that they made a complaint against Moses without cause: what was his offense and what was his sin, all the more so after they saw how much he humbled himself before Dathan and Abiram — perhaps they would return, etc. — this would show that he exerted himself so they would not die. Yet the congregation's murmuring was about what Moses did, the test of the incense all together, for he should have done the test with Korah alone, and when HaShem executed judgment upon him, the two hundred and fifty princes of the congregation would not have drawn near and would not have died. And this is the meaning of <b>saying: You have killed</b> etc. — meaning, by your statement that you said to them: ״קְחוּ אִישׁ מַחְתָּתוֹ וְגוֹ״ חֲמִשִּׁים וּמָאתַיִם — through this you killed the people of HaShem. And the congregation did not murmur about the death of Korah, Dathan, and Abiram, but about the two hundred and fifty, all of whom were heads of sanhedrin courts. And according to the words of our Sages of blessed memory, who said that the congregation's murmuring was because he commanded them to offer incense, which is a more holy and stringent service, and he did not perform the test with one of the other services — this too may be explained along the same line: <b>saying: You have killed</b>, meaning, by your statement that you told them to offer incense, you were the cause that they died."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:40.068184029Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}